From 3d21e2de6b9ed189ad501343c254ef6f83beda1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juansolo457 <5344231+Juansolo457@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:51:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Aim assist: Halo CE's model for Full (Wide) on three weapons

pm_AimAssist 3 now runs Halo CE's aim assist (OpenCE aim_assist.c and
player_control.c) for the weapons tuned from it, with the Xbox maps' values:
the blaster as the pistol (autoaim 3 degrees, magnetism 6, 30 world units),
the machinegun as the assault rifle (6/12, 25) and the shotgun (6/12, 15).
A Halo world unit is 120 Quake 4 units.

- Falloff: full strength to half of each cone's angle and distance, then
  linear to nothing at the edge. Zoom divides the angles and multiplies the
  distances by the magnification.
- Aim point: the spot on a capsule inside the target's bounds nearest the
  crosshair, pulled onto the aim line when it passes through the body.
- Shot bend: from the crosshair toward that point by the autoaim level,
  capped at the autoaim angle. A crosshair already on the target or an ally
  leaves the shot alone.
- Magnetism: the look stick slows by level x pm_AimAssistFriction (0.6), and
  while either stick is used the view follows the target's motion across it
  by level x pm_AimAssistAdhesion (0.7), capped at Halo's 180 and 90 degrees
  a second. The game sends it to the engine through pm_joystickAdhesionYaw and
  pm_joystickAdhesionPitch, cleared each player think.

Other weapons keep the wide 360 assist in mode 3, and mode 2 is unchanged.
pm_AimAssistHaloScale scales Halo's angles. testMuzzleAim prints the weapon
and the Halo levels; the help line describes the new Wide.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
